          "presentation": {
            "layout": "opener"
          },
          "movement": "spatial",
          "preset": "opener-v1",
          "titleStyle": "display",
          "text": "About Me",
          "description": "Hi, I’m Alex. I’m a designer because I see possibility in how things work—and how they could work better."
        },
        {
          "id": "text-complexity-idea",
          "kind": "title",
          "startWU": 1.4,
          "focusWU": 1.8,
          "endWU": 2.2,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 0.8,
            "gapAfter": "tight",
            "focusMode": "middle"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "center"
          },
          "movement": "spatial",
          "preset": "travelling-title-v1",
          "titleStyle": "standard",
          "text": "I’ve always been drawn to complex problems…"
        },
        {
          "id": "text-complexity-conditions",
          "kind": "title",
          "startWU": 2.55,
          "focusWU": 2.95,
          "endWU": 3.35,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 0.8,
            "gapAfter": "standard",
            "focusMode": "middle"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "center"
          },
          "movement": "spatial",
          "preset": "travelling-title-v1",
          "titleStyle": "standard",
          "text": "…especially those that refuse to stay within one discipline."
        },
        {
          "id": "text-background-unit",
          "kind": "scroll-block",
          "startWU": 3.6,
          "focusWU": 4.1,
          "endWU": 7.05,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 1.8,
            "gapAfter": "standard",
            "focusMode": "reading-start"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "reading"
          },
          "block": {
            "id": "background-unit",
            "kind": "stack",
            "modules": [
              {
                "id": "context",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "What do I mean by a complex problem? The ground is always shifting. A technology such as AI or digital identity can be useful before people are ready to trust it. A new product can ask for an interaction no one has learned yet. An ordinary tool—the phone keyboard, a consent screen, a sign-in flow—can shape millions of decisions without attracting attention."
              },
              {
                "id": "context-emphasis",
                "kind": "list",
                "items": [
                  "That is where I see the most potential for useful innovation."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "understanding",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "I want to understand what sits beneath the surface: technical constraints, human behaviour, business goals and the small details that shape an experience. The answer might be to simplify, explain something differently, or add a moment of friction—a pause before someone shares sensitive information. When design works, it can disappear into the experience. That is a good thing."
              },
              {
                "id": "education",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "I started my career in Communication Design in Mainz, Germany, around thirteen years ago. Technology interested me, but visual communication showed me how a single image, word, type choice or movement can change what someone understands and feels. That still fascinates me, and it remains fundamental to how I work."
              },
              {
                "id": "practice",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "In creative agencies I moved towards interface design, motion, design systems and close collaboration with developers. At Yoti in London, the challenge was more delicate: use product design and brand to help people trust digital identity. That was when I stopped treating product, brand and communication as separate disciplines. They solve different parts of the same problem, and they work best in service of one another."
              },
              {
                "id": "selected-clients",
                "kind": "logo-grid",
                "label": "I’ve been fortunate to work with influential organisations across automotive, aviation, charity, finance and technology.",
                "items": [
                  {
