          "preset": "travelling-title-v1",
          "titleStyle": "standard",
          "text": "The more complex the question…"
        },
        {
          "id": "text-complexity-listen",
          "kind": "title",
          "startWU": 8.05,
          "focusWU": 8.45,
          "endWU": 8.85,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 0.8,
            "gapAfter": "standard",
            "focusMode": "middle"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "center"
          },
          "movement": "spatial",
          "preset": "travelling-title-v1",
          "titleStyle": "standard",
          "text": "…the more often I work at the intersection of disciplines."
        },
        {
          "id": "text-discipline-labels",
          "kind": "scroll-block",
          "startWU": 8.95,
          "focusWU": 9.7,
          "endWU": 11.4,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 1.6,
            "gapAfter": "standard",
            "focusMode": "reading-start"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "disciplines"
          },
          "block": {
            "id": "discipline-labels",
            "kind": "disciplines",
            "label": "Disciplines",
            "items": [
              {
                "id": "product-design",
                "label": "Product Design",
                "description": "I turn ambiguous product problems into interfaces teams can build, test, and improve."
              },
              {
                "id": "experience-design",
                "label": "Experience Design",
                "description": "I connect user needs, product priorities, and the decisions that shape the journey."
              },
              {
                "id": "art-direction",
                "label": "Art Direction",
                "description": "I define the visual point of view that gives the work character, clarity, and intent."
              },
              {
                "id": "motion-and-3d",
                "label": "Motion & 3D",
                "description": "I use motion and spatial prototypes to clarify ideas, interactions, and product stories."
              },
              {
                "id": "creative-engineering",
                "label": "Creative Engineering",
                "description": "I prototype with code and AI to move decisions from discussion into working form."
              },
              {
                "id": "parametric-systems",
                "label": "Parametric Systems",
                "description": "I build systems of tokens, rules, and patterns that scale without losing character."
              }
            ]
          },
          "reveal": {
            "fadeDurationWU": 0.2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-disciplines-title",
          "kind": "scroll-block",
          "startWU": 11.5,
          "focusWU": 12.1,
          "endWU": 14.4,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
            "minScreens": 1.8,
            "gapAfter": "chapter",
            "focusMode": "reading-start"
          },
          "presentation": {
            "layout": "disciplines"
          },
          "block": {
            "id": "disciplines-passage",
            "kind": "stack",
            "modules": [
              {
                "id": "attention",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "When I begin a project, I want to understand the business, the people and the space around the problem before deciding what the work should become. A brief may name the visible problem. It rarely explains the forces that created it."
              },
              {
                "id": "brief-emphasis",
                "kind": "list",
                "items": [
                  "Good design does not always make things easier."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "friction-judgement",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "We live in a time of frictionless products and instant answers. I don’t believe less is always more. Sometimes design should slow someone down, make a decision visible or leave complexity intact. A confirmation before sharing an identity can be useful friction if it helps someone understand what they are doing."
              },
              {
                "id": "trend-judgement",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "I use trends when they help people enter something new. I distrust them when they replace the idea. An interface can look current and still have nothing to say. I would rather make something that belongs to the problem and lasts beyond the moment."
              },
              {
                "id": "making-early",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "I make things early and stay close to development. A prototype reveals where an idea is useful and where it is only decoration. Systems matter, but standardise every unusual decision and the result becomes another copy of a copy. The structure should be reliable. The important moments should still feel made by a person."
              },
              {
                "id": "ai-judgement",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "AI sharpens the same tension. It helps me explore further and make ideas visible sooner. It can also average them into something merely plausible. I use it to widen the search. Deciding what is worth making is still my responsibility."
              },
              {
                "id": "ambitious-teams",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "Not everything starts with a client. Some projects begin with a question I can’t leave alone: could a phone keyboard work better? How should people understand AI? What makes a digital product feel trustworthy? Others lead into robotics or creative engineering."
              },
              {
                "id": "unfinished-projects",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "Some become things I can share; others remain sketches, prototypes or half-answered questions. All of them shape what I do next."
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-life-momentum",
          "kind": "title",
          "startWU": 14.5,
          "focusWU": 14.85,
          "endWU": 15.2,
          "publishable": true,
          "flow": {
